 The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions." 13194139534496 17592186045417 false] [17592186345114 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nIII. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions." 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186345114 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+13{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 13 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true." 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186345114 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+13{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 13 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true." 13194139534496 17592186045417 false] [17592186423125 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423125 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423125 1083 #uuid "7050fb91-1292-55db-a723-6b10871d549b" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423126 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423126 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423126 1083 #uuid "890d24d3-277e-573f-bd96-f9cd085be63c" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423127 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423127 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423127 1083 #uuid "b04b7c67-afe2-54cf-b975-96b89dadd4bb" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423128 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423128 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423128 1083 #uuid "b45778ba-88bf-5081-bbc6-5607a701b6b7" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423129 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423129 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423129 1083 #uuid "f6f9c0c9-0094-5c66-aedb-fd4afa5ddc63" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423125 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423126 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423127 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423128 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423129 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1077 "selection" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423125 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423130 1079 #uuid "61fa1660-27f5-5adf-a8fa-9ff9b781990b" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423131 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423130 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423131 1069 "q-105290" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423131 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423131 1071 "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423131 1072 #uuid "80e0e487-e8a8-5a08-9b5d-02833cb7fd41" 13194139534496 17592186045417 true] [17592186423131 1074 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]=3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=3{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-3{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 3{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." 13194139534496 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-7050fb91-1292-55db-a723-6b10871d549b" 17592186423125 "answer-890d24d3-277e-573f-bd96-f9cd085be63c" 17592186423126 "answer-b04b7c67-afe2-54cf-b975-96b89dadd4bb" 17592186423127 "answer-b45778ba-88bf-5081-bbc6-5607a701b6b7" 17592186423128 "answer-f6f9c0c9-0094-5c66-aedb-fd4afa5ddc63" 17592186423129 "answer-field-61fa1660-27f5-5adf-a8fa-9ff9b781990b" 17592186423130 "question-80e0e487-e8a8-5a08-9b5d-02833cb7fd41" 17592186423131} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
